s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dugramen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-18T22:15:11Z","updated_at":"2025-03-19T19:24:38Z","body":"> Also properties can unfold while hovered. It should not happen when the inspector scrolls (scrolling could just reset the unfold timer).\r\n\r\nI was gonna implement a fix today but I couldn't find a way to reliably detect a scroll in `EditorInspectorSection`. All the scroll notifications say they only fire for touch events. And `NOTIFICATION_RESIZED` and `NOTIFICATION_TRANSFORM_CHANGED` don't seem to respond to scroll either.\r\n\r\nI also noticed the scene tree has the same problem, where nodes will sometimes be inspected while hover scrolling. It should be easier to fix there, since it all happens in the same node. But I'm not sure how to handle it for folded inspector sections?\r\n\r\nEdit: Ok I think I found a way actually. EditorInspector is a scroll container, so I can access the v_scroll_bar whenever an `EditorInspectorSection` is instantiated, listen to `value_changed` and reset it then\r\n\r\nEdit 2: The changes are pushed","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2734859037/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2751451076","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103